cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this research code, please cite the SPIRAL paper and its Zenodo reproducibility archive."
title: "SPIRAL: Sparse Autoencoders for Interpretable RNA Analysis"
type: software
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-08-11
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.21891845
url: "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21891845"
repository-code: "https://github.com/SadatHossain01/SPIRAL"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - RNA language models
  - sparse autoencoders
  - mechanistic interpretability
  - RNA secondary structure
  - BiRNA-BERT
abstract: >-
  Research code for a layer-wise sparse-autoencoder analysis of the BiRNA-BERT
  RNA language model, covering sparse-autoencoder training, reconstruction and
  masked-language-model fidelity evaluation, and alignment of the learned sparse
  features with bpRNA secondary-structure annotations and RNAcentral RNA-type
  labels.
